# Gene: Go Chromedp Browser Automation

## Core Viewpoint

**4-Phase Learning Path for clawbrowser-core Development**

| Phase | Topic | Key Functions | Outcome |
|-------|-------|---------------|---------|
| 1 | chromedp Basics | NewContext, Navigate, Click, SendKeys, Screenshot, Text | Browser automation scripts |
| 2 | CDP Protocol | DOM.QuerySelector, Page.Navigate, Runtime.Evaluate, Accessibility.GetFullAXTree | Direct CDP commands |
| 3 | ARIA Snapshot | GetFullAXTree, parse nodes, generate refs | @e1, @e2, @e3... |
| 4 | CLI Wrapper | cobra, viper, fmt.Errorf, go build | Executable CLI tool |

## Reasoning Chain

1. **chromedp.Run()** → High-level API → Quick start (Phase 1)
2. **CDP Domains** → DOM/Page/Runtime/Accessibility → Deep understanding (Phase 2)
3. **AXTree parsing** → Generate refs → Core feature (Phase 3)
4. **cobra CLI** → Error handling → Delivery format (Phase 4)

## Judgment Criteria

- ✅ Phase 1: Open pages, click, screenshot, extract text
- ✅ Phase 2: Call CDP domains directly
- ✅ Phase 3: Generate @e1, @e2 refs from AXTree
- ✅ Phase 4: CLI with error handling and go build

## Application Rules

1. **Start with chromedp.Run()** - Don't build from scratch
2. **Learn CDP domains incrementally** - DOM → Page → Runtime → Accessibility
3. **Reuse existing patterns** - agent-browser for ARIA reference
4. **Test each phase** - Verify before moving to next

## Verification Commands

```bash
# Phase 1: chromedp examples
go run examples/screenshot.go
go run examples/form-fill.go
go run examples/text-extract.go

# Phase 2: CDP commands
go run cdp/dom-query.go
go run cdp/page-nav.go
go run cdp/runtime-eval.go

# Phase 3: ARIA snapshot
go run aria/snapshot-gen.go

# Phase 4: CLI tool
go build -o clawbrowser .
./clawbrowser open https://example.com
./clawbrowser screenshot page.png
```

## Completion Checklist

- [ ] Phase 1: 3 practice scripts (screenshot, form, text)
- [ ] Phase 2: CDP domain tests (DOM, Page, Runtime, Accessibility)
- [ ] Phase 3: Snapshot generator with refs
- [ ] Phase 4: Executable CLI with error handling

